From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] luma: keep notifications after short-lived app sender exits

The notification forwarder preserves the original D-Bus sender. A command
such as notify-send can exit immediately after Notify returns, while its
desktop-entry hint still resolves a real app. Keep that app's notification
source until its records expire or are dismissed; an already empty source
can still be removed when its sender vanishes.
---
diff --git a/js/ui/notificationDaemon.js b/js/ui/notificationDaemon.js
--- a/js/ui/notificationDaemon.js
+++ b/js/ui/notificationDaemon.js
@@ -432,11 +432,10 @@
     }
 
     _onNameVanished() {
-        // Destroy the notification source when its sender is removed from DBus.
-        // Only do so if this.app is set to avoid removing "notify-send" sources, senders
-        // of which аre removed from DBus immediately.
-        // Sender being removed from DBus would normally result in a tray icon being removed,
-        // so allow the code path that handles the tray icon being removed to handle that case.
-        if (this.app)
+        // A short-lived sender can name an installed app. Keep its records
+        // until their own expiry or dismissal, even after notify-send exits.
+        // Source.addNotification destroys the source when the last record
+        // goes away; an already empty app source can be removed now.
+        if (this.app && this.notifications.length === 0)
             this.destroy();
     }
